A||||7||Gerald||Best way to make the 2.8 faster||||1||
Z||000000||Gerald||11-20-2001||12:54 AM||||Well Im begining to find my duke quiet boring so I will buy a new fireo after christmas. Whats the best way to make the v6 go faster without spending an arm and a leg.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Devotshka||11-20-2001||01:15 AM||||Push it off a cliff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Seriously though... in order of cost (roughly)..<BR>Nitrous<BR>Stroke it to 3.1<BR>Turbo<BR>Supercharger (big $$$ for the only kit i've seen)<P>If you are mechanically minded you could do the 3.1 rebuild for probably less than a nitrous setup since you wouldn't have to pay any labor. <P>Other than that, theres probably a dozen little things you could do for minor increases (like exhaust manifold porting etc).||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackStang95||11-20-2001||02:29 AM||||Just keep it well maintained, good wires and plugs, k+n, fresh oil, etc, and weight down as low as possible, inflate tires just right and enjoy, thats as good as it gets for cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-20-2001||08:08 AM||||Question:  You find the duke quite (quiet?) boring, what makes you think the V6 will also be slow and needs to go faster?<P>Without spending an arm and a leg (don't know how much that is), you'll find a Fiero V6 with 250000 Km+ miles on it that will need an engine overhaul among other things.<P>The stock V6 (when new) had a top speed of 200 kph, just how fast do you need to go in Edmonton?<P>More speed = more $, simple fact.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87FieroGTx||11-20-2001||11:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Just keep it well maintained, good wires and plugs, k+n, fresh oil, etc, and weight down as low as possible, inflate tires just right and enjoy, thats as good as it gets for cheap.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I agree!<P><BR> Before you go bolting on 50-100hp NOS/Turbo make sure your engine is in top form. I say the first thing I would do is rebuild it (3.1) with the best parts I could afford OR better yet go with the superior 3.4 block then I would Turbo it!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||11-20-2001||06:23 PM||||When I get this car I do plan on an engine rebuild. How much more would it cost to stroke it to a 3.1?If I do put alot into this car I only want to spend around 2000-3000cdn on the drive train. I know that would make a turbo or super charger out of the question. Im hoping to get about the same performance as a dodge daytona turbo 2.||||reg||1
